2.9 Copying and references 

This is a common source of bugs.

a=[10,20,30]
b=a
b.append(40)
print(a)
print(b)

Output :

[10,20,30,40]
[10,20,30,40]

VERY IMPORTANT POINT -> A is changing because a and b refers to the same list.

To make a separate "shallow" copy.

Code:

a=[10,20,30]
b=a.copy()
b.append(40)
print(a)
print(b)

Output:

[10,20,30]
[10,20,30,40]

About the Code; A shallow Copy is enough for flat list. With nested lists, inner lists can be shared. For a fully independent copy of nested mutable data use "copy.deepcopy()" when appropriate.

